        <dl class="bg-bg p-5 md:p-6 font-mono text-xs md:text-sm space-y-3">
          {[
            ['Compute',   'On your phone. Every score is calculated locally.'],
            ['Account',   'None. No sign-up, no email, no login.'],
            ['Server',    'None. There is no Heart cloud to send data to.'],
            ['Telemetry', 'None. No analytics, no ads, no tracking.'],
            ['Network',   'OpenStreetMap map tiles only, plus Google Drive backup if you connect it.'],
            ['Backups',   'Automatic, to Download/Heart on your phone. They survive an uninstall.'],
            ['Maths',     'Published, cited formulas. Auditable, not a black box.'],
          ].map(([k, v]) => (
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:gap-4">
              <dt class="text-hint sm:w-28 shrink-0">{k}</dt>
              <dd class="text-primary/85 flex gap-2"><span class="text-accent hidden sm:inline" aria-hidden="true">→</span>{v}</dd>
            </div>
          ))}
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="section-reveal mb-12">
        <HeartArchitectureDiagram />
      </div>

      <!-- Validation card: the strongest credibility signal, kept visible. -->
      <div class="section-reveal mb-6 p-5 rounded-2xl bg-bg border border-accent/30">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <div aria-hidden="true" class="shrink-0 w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-accent/15 border border-accent/40 flex items-center justify-center text-base">✓</div>
          <div class="min-w-0 w-full">
            <p class="text-accent text-xs font-mono tracking-widest mb-1.5">VALIDATION · 13 ALGORITHMS · 84 TEST CASES</p>
            <p class="text-primary text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3">
              Every closed-form algorithm in Heart produces output <span class="text-accent">matching the numpy reference</span> (the backend behind pyhrv, hrv-analysis, and Kubios HRV) to floating-point precision: global maximum deviation <span class="text-accent font-mono">1.42 × 10⁻¹⁴</span>, at the IEEE-754 double-precision noise floor.
            </p>
            <p class="text-secondary text-xs leading-relaxed">
              Reproducible via <span class="text-primary/70 font-mono text-[11px] break-all">flutter test test/algorithm_validation_test.dart</span>. Because every formula is closed-form (Tanaka 2001, Uth 2004, Keytel 2005, Holt 1957, ESC/NASPE 1996, Banister 1975, Coyle 1998), "matches numpy" equals "matches Kubios" by mathematical identity.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Deep technical reference behind ONE toggle. -->
      <details class="group section-reveal rounded-2xl border border-border overflow-hidden mb-10">
        <summary class={`flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3.5 bg-surface cursor-pointer list-none [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden hover:bg-surface/60 transition-colors ${focusRing}`}>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2" aria-hidden="true">
